Z||000014||Spektyr||04-30-2001||05:31 AM||||Just wanted to pipe in here about the military.<P>Of course individual experiences vary, but as an ex-military man I'd like to strongly encourage people NOT to enlist unless you are certain you want to STAY in the military.<P>I mean think about it... if you don't like your civilian job, you can find another and then quit.  If you don't like your military job, so what -- you signed a contract!<P>Trust me, the money ain't worth it if you hate your job.  And the pay isn't very good to begin with.  I was in a very advanced field, rapid promotions and a high security clearance.  And like over 50% of the people in the enlisted ranks I lived below the poverty level.<P>Flip burgers at McDonalds if you have to.  Don't join the military unless you WANT to.||||reg||1
Z||000015||lou_dias||04-30-2001||10:05 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.cfhub.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cfhub.com</A>  is where I got that link...<BR>that's a great site and there are more links for CF jobs on there as well...<P>Lou||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cameron||05-01-2001||01:19 PM||||Thanks for the info about the military...I would tend to agree with you.<P>Lou_dias - cool thanks I'll take a look at that site.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Cameron<BR> <A HREF="http://Fiero.NetMARC.com" TARGET=_blank>http://Fiero.NetMARC.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||DaRkLoRD||05-01-2001||04:48 PM||||I agree 100% about the military.. that's why I'd never join. Another reason.. in a civilian job, you can quit if you're ordered to do something you don't want to do.. not so in the military.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>the USAF seems cool though, cause of the aircraft.. couldn't join anyway even if I wanted to, I'm Canadian.. (plus I have a heart condition and so wouldn't pass the physical.)<P>I'm not dissing people who enjoy their military service work. But I'd never want to join.. I have no notions of patriotism so strong that I'd take orders from or die for my country.. just my opinion, nothing personal towards anyone. I have several friends in the military, both canadian and american.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Spektyr||05-02-2001||05:11 AM||||I don't have a problem fighting.  Not with killing or with dying.  Given the choice I'd gladly fight a war to protect the way of life of my friends, family and fellow Americans.<P>I just couldn't deal with the realization that my country wasn't being run by patriots, and those people (most of whom had never been in the military) were giving the orders to the military.  When the US does have the honor to declare war on their enemies (which they don't usually) the war is usually being fought over money, not right and wrong.<P>Most of the time they just send American people to fight and die without the support of the American govt.<P>"Okay, you go here and do this.  By the way, don't die or get captured, because we won't acknowledge you as Americans if you do."<P>It's 'do the job right or you don't come home'.<P>I just got sick of it and told them where they could stick their hazard pay.  And no, you can't quit, but you can get out.  It just isn't very easy or very nice.  But then again, I wasn't trained to be friendly...||||reg||1
Z||000019||Taijiguy||05-02-2001||06:44 PM||||I dunno if I agree about the military or not. When I joined the pay was really low, but Reagan changed that, I was making over 1700 a month on shore duty when I got out in 87. Not alot, but certainly far above poverty level. The experience was great, but I think a person needs to have some idea of what they want to do when they enlist. I was "sold" a position by the recruiter because my test scores were high enough that I could do whatever I wanted. He convinced me to become a missile technician on a nuclear sub. Sadly, despite the glamorous picture the recruiter painted, there isn't a great deal of demand in the civilian world for a guy who can blow up entire countries.<BR>I think choosing the military depends on what you make of it.||||reg||1
